│ patch_name               │ zero_phase_kalman_savgol_filter                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially weighted moving average with a two-stage approach: (1) a 1D     │
│                          │ constant-velocity Kalman filter with adaptive measurement noise estimated from local      │
│                          │ residual variance (noise-adaptive gain), and (2) a short zero-phase Savitzky-Golay pass   │
│                          │ to suppress residual slope reversals without adding lag (Savitzky-Golay with polyorder 2  │
│                          │ preserves linear trends with no phase delay). The Kalman filter tracks the signal with    │
│                          │ minimal lag, its adaptive R reduces spurious reversals from noise spikes, and the SG      │
│                          │ polynomial fit preserves genuine dynamics. We keep the same output-length semantics       │
│                          │ (len(x) - window_size + 1) and the existing function signatures so `process_signal` and   │
│                          │ `run_signal_processing` remain unchanged. Moving-average baselines are kept as fallbacks  │
│                          │ for compatibility.                                                                        │
