│ patch_name               │ kalman_trend_guard_filter                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Redesigns the pipeline around a three-stage streaming architecture: (1) an adaptive 1D    │
│                          │ Kalman filter (state = ) whose process noise auto-tunes to local volatility, (2) a        │
│                          │ polynomial (Savitzky-Golay-style) trend refinement stage that preserves dynamics with low │
│                          │ phase lag, and (3) a trend-guard / hysteresis stage that suppresses spurious slope        │
│                          │ reversals (false reversals) by requiring a slope change to exceed an adaptive threshold.  │
│                          │ The whole filter is vectorized and computes outputs in one pass, keeping efficiency high  │
│                          │ while dramatically reducing slope changes, false reversals, lag error, and average error  │
│                          │ compared to a moving average. Public API (process_signal, run_signal_processing,          │
│                          │ generate_test_signal) and output formats are unchanged; only the internal filtering is    │
│                          │ replaced with the modular pipeline.                                                       │
