│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_kalman_zero_phase_filter                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially-weighted moving average with an adaptive 1D Kalman filter       │
│                          │ combined with a zero-phase forward/backward pass and trend-aware (constant-velocity)      │
│                          │ state model. A Kalman filter with a velocity state tracks trends better than any windowed │
│                          │ average (drastically lower lag error), while adaptive measurement-noise estimation (via   │
│                          │ innovation-based noise floor tracking) suppresses spurious slope reversals and false      │
│                          │ reversals. The forward-backward (RTS-style smoothing) pass removes phase delay, improving │
│                          │ responsiveness, correlation, and tracking accuracy while keeping O(N) complexity          │
│                          │ (efficiency stays high). The output length is kept identical to the original              │
│                          │ sliding-window output (len(x) - window_size + 1) for API compatibility, with outputs      │
│                          │ aligned to window centers so the alignment in run_signal_processing is correct (delay     │
│                          │ already accounted for there).                                                             │
