│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_adaptive_filter                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the weighted moving average with a zero-lag adaptive Kalman filter combined with  │
│                          │ adaptive process noise. A steady-state 1D Kalman filter has essentially zero phase delay  │
│                          │ (unlike the moving average which lags by ~(W-1)/2 samples), directly improving lag_error  │
│                          │ and tracking accuracy. The process noise Q is adapted online from the local signal        │
│                          │ variance so fast trends are tracked (responsiveness) while noise is suppressed when the   │
│                          │ signal is quiet — reducing slope changes and false reversals. Additionally, a two-pass    │
│                          │ forward/backward smoothing is avoided to keep it causal/real-time; instead the            │
│                          │ measurement noise R is estimated from local high-frequency residual variance. Output      │
│                          │ length must remain len(x)-window_size+1 for compatibility, so the filter runs over the    │
│                          │ full signal and the last (output_length) samples are returned, which minimizes alignment  │
│                          │ delay (delay becomes ~0 effectively).                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
