│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_adaptive_filter                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially-weighted moving average with an adaptive Kalman filter with     │
│                          │ online trend (velocity) tracking. A constant-velocity Kalman model estimates both level   │
│                          │ and slope each step, so it anticipates trends instead of lagging behind them (reducing    │
│                          │ lag error), while the measurement-noise vs process-noise ratio (adapted from residual     │
│                          │ statistics) provides strong smoothing that suppresses spurious slope changes and false    │
│                          │ reversals. This directly targets all four objectives: slope change minimization, lag      │
│                          │ minimization, tracking accuracy, and false reversal penalty. The filter is O(1) per       │
│                          │ sample, keeping execution time low. We keep the same output length convention as before   │
│                          │ for compatibility, but align estimates with the end of each causal window so phase delay  │
│                          │ is minimal.                                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
