│ patch_name               │ adaptive_trend_pipeline_filter                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign from a monolithic sliding-window filter into a modular streaming      │
│                          │ pipeline with pluggable stages. Data flows through: (1) an adaptive Kalman smoothing      │
│                          │ stage whose noise covariance adapts to innovation magnitude, (2) a slope estimator using  │
│                          │ local polynomial regression on the Kalman state, (3) a hysteresis-based trend classifier  │
│                          │ that suppresses false reversals, and (4) a zero-lag blend that phase-corrects the         │
│                          │ smoothed estimate back toward the raw signal. Each stage is an independent class          │
│                          │ implementing a common `process(sample) -> state` interface, wired by a `Pipeline`         │
│                          │ orchestrator, enabling easy substitution (e.g., swap Kalman for particle filter). This    │
│                          │ improves maintainability, testability, and lets each optimization objective be isolated   │
│                          │ and tuned independently, while the phase-compensation stage explicitly targets lag error  │
│                          │ rather than treating it implicitly.                                                       │
