│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ triple_sg_adaptive_pipeline                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign around a composable multi-stage filtering pipeline. Each filtering    │
│                          │ stage is a self-contained module implementing a common `FilterStage` interface            │
│                          │ (`apply(signal) -> filtered`), orchestrated by a `SignalPipeline` class that chains       │
│                          │ stages. This replaces the monolithic function body with: (1) reflection-padded zero-phase │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay stage (used three times with progressively smaller windows — the third     │
│                          │ pass directly attacks the weakest smoothness metric), (2) a slope-stabilization stage     │
│                          │ that suppresses spurious directional reversals by majority-vote over local slope signs,   │
│                          │ and (3) a trend-locking stage using local linear regression to preserve genuine trend     │
│                          │ dynamics and penalize false reversals. The zero-phase construction (row-0 of              │
│                          │ pinv(AᵀA)·Aᵀ) is retained per stage, so lag error stays controlled while noise reduction  │
│                          │ scales with stage count. The pipeline architecture improves maintainability (stages       │
│                          │ tunable independently), efficiency (precomputed convolution kernels), and allows          │
│                          │ per-stage re-measurement of the four objectives.                                          │
