│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ kalman_rts_hysteresis_filter                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The best prior program (score 0.62) was the constant-acceleration Kalman filter with an   │
│                          │ RTS backward smoother. The current version's added slope-based lead compensation and      │
│                          │ global Savitzky-Golay polish actually degraded performance (noise_reduction 0.83→0.33,    │
│                          │ correlation 0.97→0.92) because the lead reintroduced noise and the SG pass was applied    │
│                          │ everywhere. The new program reverts to the strong Kalman+RTS core and, inspired by the    │
│                          │ reversal-suppression hysteresis recommendation, adds a *localized* post-stage: it         │
│                          │ computes the gradient of the smoothed output, flags only short neighborhoods where the    │
│                          │ gradient sign flips within a few samples while the gradient magnitude is below a fraction │
│                          │ of the median gradient magnitude (residual micro-oscillations), and applies a tiny        │
│                          │ zero-phase order-2 Savitzky-Golay pass only inside those flagged neighborhoods. This      │
│                          │ directly targets slope_changes and false_reversals without disturbing the well-performing │
│                          │ trend structure elsewhere.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
