│ patch_description        │ Replace the exponentially-weighted moving average with a multi-stage pipeline: (1)        │
│                          │ estimate local noise via rolling residual standard deviation, (2) apply a Savitzky-Golay  │
│                          │ style zero-phase polynomial smoothing convolution (which preserves polynomial trends up   │
│                          │ to order 2 exactly, minimizing lag and tracking error, unlike the moving average that     │
│                          │ attenuates amplitude and introduces phase delay), and (3) make the half-window locally    │
│                          │ adaptive in blocks based on local volatility — wide windows in noisy segments to suppress │
│                          │ slope changes/false reversals, narrow windows in quiet segments to preserve               │
│                          │ responsiveness. Output length is kept consistent with the current contract (len(x) -      │
│                          │ window_size + 1) so external code still works. All stages are convolution-based (O(n)),   │
│                          │ preserving efficiency_score 1.00.                                                         │
