│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the current best (0.59: adaptive constant-velocity Kalman prefilter + fixed  │
│                          │ zero-phase SG smoother) with the 0.58 inspiration script (locally-adaptive multi-scale SG │
│                          │ blending driven by local volatility). The new filter keeps the Kalman prefilter with      │
│                          │ robust 3σ innovation gating, then replaces the single fixed-scale SG stage with a         │
│                          │ volatility-driven soft blend of three zero-phase SG scales (narrow/medium/wide, weighted  │
│                          │ by Gaussian membership of local volatility at 20/50/80 percentiles). Wide scales activate │
│                          │ where noise is high (fewer spurious slope reversals, better smoothness/noise reduction),  │
│                          │ narrow scales dominate where the signal is quiet (preserving responsiveness and genuine   │
│                          │ turning points). Additionally, a light slope-based lead compensation (using a low-pass    │
│                          │ filtered slope channel) recovers lag without amplifying noise. All stages are O(n)        │
│                          │ convolutions; end-aligned trim preserves the sliding-window output contract.              │
