│ patch_description        │ Builds on the best-performing generation (Kalman constant-acceleration filter + RTS       │
│                          │ backward smoother + localized hysteresis, score 0.63). Key insight from the               │
│                          │ recommendations: trend-compensation lead reduces lag_error, but only if the slope used    │
│                          │ for the lead comes from a denoised source. Prior failure (Gen 16's 66.4 false reversals)  │
│                          │ came from computing the lead via np.gradient(smoothed), which re-injected high-frequency  │
│                          │ ripple. Here, I advance each RTS-smoothed estimate along its own Kalman/RTS slope state   │
│                          │ (smoothed[:,1]) with lead = 0.4 × (window_size//4). Since the RTS slope state is          │
│                          │ model-smoothed, the compensation adds no new reversals while cutting lag. The localized   │
│                          │ weak-flip hysteresis stage then cleans up any residual micro-oscillations. Output         │
│                          │ contract preserved: end-aligned, length n − window_size + 1.                              │
