│ patch_description        │ The current version (Gen 5) removed the trend-compensation lead and improved (0.63,       │
│                          │ lag_error 0.26). Prior evidence: adding lead with a raw gradient (Gen 3's np.gradient     │
│                          │ style) reintroduced ripple; but using the RTS-smoothed Kalman slope state as the lead     │
│                          │ source gave the best false-reversal behavior among lead variants. Recommendation: re-add  │
│                          │ the predictive lead at 0.4×sg_half, but compute it from `smoothed[:, 1]` (the denoised    │
│                          │ RTS slope state), and additionally apply a short SG polish to the slope state itself      │
│                          │ before the lead multiplication to remove any residual curvature ripple. This should       │
│                          │ reduce lag_error below 0.26 while keeping the 0.97 correlation and improving false        │
│                          │ reversals, since the lead is driven entirely by model-smoothed, low-frequency slope       │
│                          │ information rather than a raw gradient.                                                   │
