│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rts_smoother_on_2state_kf                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Prior programs show the 2-state  Kalman with Q = 0.05·(median|diff|)² is a proven winner, │
│                          │ and Gens 25/32 showed an RTS backward smoother pass reduces lag error (0.31 vs 0.35) and  │
│                          │ noise while matching correlation 0.94 — they lost only because of aggressive              │
│                          │ lead/hysteresis add-ons and the jitter-inducing 3-state model. This edit: (1) stores the  │
│                          │ filtered states and covariances (and predicted covariances) during the existing forward   │
│                          │ Kalman loop, (2) adds a standard RTS backward recursion on the  state, and (3) feeds the  │
│                          │ smoothed level channel into the existing multi-scale SG stage, which stays unchanged. The │
│                          │ RTS pass uses full forward+backward evidence, so it removes noise-induced wobble (fewer   │
│                          │ false reversals / slope changes) without adding lag the way a wider forward window would. │
│                          │ We deliberately avoid slope-lead compensation, which hurt smoothness in Gens 25/26/28/32. │
