│                          │ the slope-lead compensation stage, which degrades noise reduction and increases lag error │
│                          │ in the other variants. This crossover therefore combines the reversal-gated Kalman core   │
│                          │ and RTS smoother from the top-scoring script with the zero-phase local hysteresis stage   │
│                          │ shared across all high performers, drops the lead stage that hurt the 0.55–0.58 variants, │
│                          │ and keeps the end-aligned output contract (n - window_size + 1). The gross-outlier Huber  │
│                          │ guard on the measurement covariance is retained for robustness, and the SG coefficients   │
│                          │ are precomputed for efficiency.                                                           │
