│ patch_description        │ Replace the filtering-only Kalman pass with a forward Kalman + Rauch-Tung-Striebel (RTS)  │
│                          │ backward smoother on the  state. Gens 25/32 showed this beats the current best on lag     │
│                          │ error (0.31 vs 0.35) and noise reduction while matching correlation 0.94; the only        │
│                          │ weakness was smoothness, caused by aggressive lead/hysteresis add-ons — so we keep the    │
│                          │ proven Gen 7 post-stages exactly: double zero-phase Savitzky-Golay, a conservative        │
│                          │ slope-lead compensation (0.25·0.5·sg_half), and end-aligned trimming. We store s, P, and  │
│                          │ the predicted s_pred, P_pred during the forward loop, then run the standard RTS           │
│                          │ recursion: s_smooth = s_filt + G(s_smooth − s_pred) with G = P_filt Fᵀ P_pred⁻¹. Q stays  │
│                          │ at 0.05·(median|diff|)² and the 2-state constant-velocity model is retained, since        │
│                          │ 3-state variants with reversal gates injected jitter in Gens 25/26/28/32. The robust      │
│                          │ innovation gating and adaptive R from the current program are preserved. This combines    │
│                          │ the two proven winners: RTS's lag/noise advantage plus Gen 7's smoothness stages, without │
│                          │ the failed extras.                                                                        │
