│ patch_description        │ The metrics show the pipeline already achieves good lag (0.35), correlation (0.95), and   │
│                          │ accuracy (0.95), but smoothness (0.29) and slope changes (48.40) / false reversals        │
│                          │ (34.80) are the weak points. Two targeted improvements: (1) The Stage 4 lead compensation │
│                          │ currently uses `np.gradient(smoothed)` on the doubly-SG-smoothed signal — but the RTS     │
│                          │ smoother already produced an optimal, low-noise *smoothed slope* estimate (second state). │
│                          │ Using that slope for the lead term both restores dynamics more faithfully and injects far │
│                          │ less residual noise back into the output, directly reducing slope reversals. A small      │
│                          │ zero-phase SG polish of that slope suppresses remaining jitter. (2) Add a reversal gate:  │
│                          │ where the slope magnitude is small relative to local volatility (i.e., trend is not       │
│                          │ statistically meaningful), zero the lead term — this prevents the lead compensation from  │
│                          │ manufacturing false reversals in flat/noisy regions, cutting false_reversals while        │
│                          │ keeping the responsiveness gain where a genuine trend exists. Q, the 2-state model, and   │
│                          │ the proven SG/RTS structure are untouched.                                                │
