│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ widen_widest_sg_scale                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current 3-scale SG bank uses half-widths {sg_half//2, sg_half, 3·sg_half//2}. The     │
│                          │ widest kernel dominates oscillation suppression in volatile regions, which is the direct  │
│                          │ lever on the 44.4 false-reversal / 65.8 slope-change bottleneck. The 3/2·sg_half cap was  │
│                          │ chosen once and never tuned, so it is the least-explored knob. Widening the widest scale  │
│                          │ to 2·sg_half gives the volatility-gated branch a stronger smoothing option exactly where  │
│                          │ local noise is highest (soft Gaussian membership ensures it only engages in               │
│                          │ high-volatility samples, so quiet regions keep their responsiveness and lag_error is      │
│                          │ unaffected). This is a single-parameter change: keep the other two scales and all         │
│                          │ weighting/percentile logic intact. Order-2 SG remains zero-phase and reproduces genuine   │
│                          │ quadratic turning points, so tracking accuracy is preserved even at the wider kernel.     │
│                          │ Since half-widths grow, the reflect-padding and degenerate-length guards already in       │
│                          │ _sg_smooth handle short signals safely, and output length remains n - window_size + 1 via │
│                          │ the existing end-aligned trim.                                                            │
