│                          │ the best-performing prior generation, but the process noise is now scheduled by local     │
│                          │ volatility. A rolling MAD-based local volatility estimate v_i is computed from first      │
│                          │ differences; Q_i = 0.05·med_diff²·(1 + v_i/median(v)) lets the filter stay rigid in quiet │
│                          │ regions (fewer false reversals and slope changes) while tracking fast genuine dynamics    │
│                          │ (lower lag error, better responsiveness). Measurement outlier gating and the RTS smoother │
│                          │ recursion (np.linalg.solve-based) are unchanged. No curvature state (failed in three      │
│                          │ rounds), no slope lead (regressed the current program), keeping the localized             │
│                          │ reversal-suppression hysteresis as the final stage.                                       │
