│                          │ 1]` before it is overwritten), which is a far cleaner trend estimate than numerically     │
│                          │ differencing the final output (the approach that failed in Gen 41 with 85.4 false         │
│                          │ reversals). We (1) capture the RTS slope state before the SG stage reuses the variable,   │
│                          │ (2) apply one short 5-tap SG pass to strip any residual ripple from the slope channel,    │
│                          │ and (3) advance the output by a conservative `lead = 0.2 * sg_half * slope_smoothed`      │
│                          │ samples-worth of level. This shifts the level forward along its own denoised trend        │
│                          │ direction, directly reducing lag_error (currently 0.27) with minimal added distortion,    │
│                          │ since the slope channel is already heavily denoised by both the RTS smoother and the      │
│                          │ extra 5-tap pass. Fewer spurious reversals should also result because the lead is         │
│                          │ proportional to a clean slope rather than a noisy one, and the small coefficient          │
│                          │ (0.2·sg_half) keeps the extrapolation local.                                              │
