│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tv_trend_lead_filter                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Fundamentally different approach: replace the Kalman/RTS machinery with an ℓ1             │
│                          │ total-variation (TV) trend filter solved by Condat's fast primal-dual algorithm. TV       │
│                          │ denoising is the classic solution to exactly this problem class: it produces              │
│                          │ piecewise-linear estimates with the minimum number of slope changes, directly optimizing  │
│                          │ slope-change and false-reversal metrics, while its edge-preserving property avoids the    │
│                          │ lag/oversmoothing trade-off that penalizes Kalman and moving-average filters. A small     │
│                          │ trend-gated lead compensation (advancing the estimate along its own piecewise slope)      │
│                          │ offsets the residual smoothing lag, boosting responsiveness. TV filtering is O(n), robust │
│                          │ to non-stationarity (no stationarity assumption, no noise model required beyond a scale   │
│                          │ estimate), and the convex formulation guarantees a unique, stable solution. The output    │
│                          │ contract (length n - window_size + 1, end-aligned) is preserved exactly.                  │
