│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ qscheduled_rts_trend_filter                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Implements the recommended Q-scheduling: the 2-state constant-velocity Kalman filter's    │
│                          │ process noise is now scaled per-step by local volatility, symmetrically with the          │
│                          │ already-winning volatility-adaptive R. Q_i = 0.05·q_scale²·(1 + v_i/median(v)) lets the   │
│                          │ filter stay rigid (fewer false reversals, better smoothness) in quiet regions while       │
│                          │ opening up to track genuine fast dynamics (lower lag error, better responsiveness). Keeps │
│                          │ the np.linalg.solve-based RTS smoother and volatility-blended multi-scale zero-phase SG   │
│                          │ polish exactly as-is (no curvature state). Drops the risky slope-lead extrapolation that  │
│                          │ hurt false reversals in the current generation, relying instead on the flexible Q for     │
│                          │ responsiveness.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
