│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sigmoid_gated_slope_lead_on_rts_slope                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The two prior champions each peaked at 0.65 on opposite ends of the trade-off:            │
│                          │ lag_error=0.27 with high noise, and smoothness/false-reversals with lag. The hybrid       │
│                          │ composition keeps the current Kalman+RTS adaptive-R 3σ-gated backbone (which delivered    │
│                          │ lag 0.27) and adds the missing pieces: (1) keep the percentile-blended multi-scale SG     │
│                          │ (already present), (2) add a slope-lead compensation term driven by the *RTS smoothed     │
│                          │ slope* (the optimal low-noise derivative estimate, far less noisy than finite             │
│                          │ differences, so it restores dynamics without re-creating spurious reversals), gated by a  │
│                          │ *smooth sigmoid* in |slope| space rather than a hard binary gate — the hard gate causes   │
│                          │ discontinuities at the threshold that themselves register as slope changes. The lead      │
│                          │ magnitude is a modest fraction of the SG half-window, applied only where the trend is     │
│                          │ statistically meaningful relative to local noise scale. This attacks lag_error (still     │
│                          │ 0.27) while the sigmoid gating + already-achieved noise reduction (0.82) protects         │
│                          │ smoothness and false reversals, aiming to break the 0.65 plateau on the composite.        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0106                                                                                   │
