│                          │ Gen 46: smoothness 0.30 / false reversals 34). Stage 1: constant-velocity Kalman forward  │
│                          │ pass with volatility-adaptive R and 3σ innovation gating (from Gen 45), using             │
│                          │ linalg.solve-based RTS backward smoothing for stable low-noise level+slope states. Stage  │
│                          │ 2: multi-scale zero-phase Savitzky-Golay with three half-widths blended by soft Gaussian  │
│                          │ weights on local volatility centered at 20/50/80 percentiles (from Gen 46) — wide windows │
│                          │ kill false reversals in volatile regions while narrow windows preserve responsiveness.    │
│                          │ Stage 3: novel sigmoid-gated slope-lead compensation driven by the RTS smoothed slope     │
│                          │ (low-noise derivative), where a smooth sigmoid gate (rather than a hard binary gate)      │
│                          │ blends the lead in proportion to the slope's statistical significance — restoring         │
│                          │ dynamics killed by double smoothing without manufacturing spurious reversals. Stage 4:    │
│                          │ end-aligned trim to sliding-window output length.                                         │
