│ patch_description        │ The current program's bottleneck is smoothness (0.36) and slope changes (36) / false      │
│                          │ reversals (29), while responsiveness (0.71) and lag (0.41) are acceptable. The lead       │
│                          │ compensation in Stage 4 reintroduces some residual oscillation into the smoothed signal.  │
│                          │ Adding a light, unconditional third SG pass (half = max(2, sg_half//3), order 2) after    │
│                          │ the lead compensation — before the trim — suppresses these residual oscillations at       │
│                          │ negligible lag cost, since the pass is zero-phase (no group delay) and its window is      │
│                          │ short. We reuse `_zero_phase_smooth` verbatim (it already handles reflect padding and     │
│                          │ degenerate lengths) and validate the output length after the pass as a safety net. This   │
│                          │ directly targets the remaining headroom in smoothness and false reversals without         │
│                          │ sacrificing the already-strong correlation/responsiveness tradeoff.                       │
