│ patch_description        │ Replace the explicit matrix inverse in the RTS smoother gain with a numerically more      │
│                          │ stable solve-based formulation, G = solve(Pm^T, (P_filt @ F^T)^T)^T. This is equivalent   │
│                          │ mathematically but avoids ill-conditioned inversions of the predicted covariance, which   │
│                          │ historically (Gen 35) yielded more stable and smoother RTS passes. Q stays strictly fixed │
│                          │ at 0.05·q_scale² — Q-scheduling by volatility was confirmed across four rounds (Gens 53,  │
│                          │ 54, 59, 61) to degrade smoothness and inflate reversals, so no change is made there. The  │
│                          │ 3-state CA model and TV/Condat filtering remain excluded as confirmed dead ends. This is  │
│                          │ a zero-cost numerical-stability improvement targeting slope_changes/false_reversals       │
│                          │ without touching lag or accuracy.                                                         │
