│ patch_description        │ Structural redesign as a two-branch composition: (A) a percentile-blended 3-scale         │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay kernel bank (half-widths sg/2, sg, 2·sg) weighted by Gaussian kernels      │
│                          │ centered at the 20/50/80th percentiles of local robust volatility, and (B) an             │
│                          │ RTS-smoothed 2-state Kalman whose smoothed slope gates a small lead compensation          │
│                          │ (RTS-slope lead) to reduce lag. Outputs are blended and passed through the localized      │
│                          │ reversal-suppression hysteresis. This decouples "smoothing strength" (kernel bank) from   │
│                          │ "responsiveness" (slope-gated lead), modularizing each objective into its own stage       │
│                          │ instead of the monolithic Kalman+hysteresis chain.                                        │
