│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tvf_emd_hybrid                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ A fundamentally different approach: total-variation denoising (TVF) with an L1 wavelet    │
│                          │ regularizer. TVF is a sparse-derivative filter that is provably edge-preserving — it      │
│                          │ removes noise without blurring turning points, directly attacking slope_changes and       │
│                          │ false_reversals while keeping lag near zero. We solve the fused-lasso problem with a fast │
│                          │ taut-string algorithm (O(n) in expectation), which produces a piecewise-linear estimate   │
│                          │ whose derivative changes only at statistically significant points. A wavelet-shrinkage    │
│                          │ residual polish and mild slope lead finish the pipeline. Unlike the Kalman+SG family      │
│                          │ (Gaussian smoothers that must trade lag vs. reversals), the taut string's 1D structure    │
│                          │ gives hard reversals only at genuine trend breaks.                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
