│ patch_description        │ Composition of the two strongest prior generations: a percentile-blended 3-scale          │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay kernel bank (half-widths , Gaussian weights centered at the 20/50/80th     │
│                          │ percentiles of local volatility) applied on top of the RTS-smoothed Kalman level,         │
│                          │ combined with the confidence-gated trend lead from Gen 45 (the 0.63 combined-score anchor │
│                          │ with lag 0.30) and the volatility-scheduled Q from Gen 46. The wider third scale          │
│                          │ (2·sg_half instead of 1.5·sg_half) increases smoothing depth in volatile regions, further │
│                          │ reducing noise reduction error and slope reversals, while the tanh confidence gate on the │
│                          │ MAD-scaled slope channel advances only statistically significant trends — keeping lag low │
│                          │ where it matters and flat where the signal is quiet. All stages are O(n) convolutions and │
│                          │ 2×2 matrix recursions, preserving the 1.00 efficiency score.                              │
