│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sg_kernel_bank_rts_slope_lead                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This edit composes the Gen 45 percentile-blended 3-scale Savitzky-Golay kernel bank       │
│                          │ (half-widths  with Gaussian volatility-membership weights at the 20/50/80th percentiles   │
│                          │ of local volatility, which achieved noise reduction 0.82 and smoothness on its own) with  │
│                          │ the current constant-acceleration Kalman + RTS + reversal-gate pipeline. The current      │
│                          │ best's smoothness is only 0.20 and slope_changes ~80, driven by residual                  │
│                          │ micro-oscillations in the smoothed level. A multi-scale zero-phase SG bank applied to the │
│                          │ RTS output suppresses those oscillations aggressively (biggest half-width = 2*sg_half)    │
│                          │ while the percentile-matched Gaussian weights keep narrow windows on quiet segments,      │
│                          │ preserving responsiveness (lag stays bounded because the SG is zero-phase). To compensate │
│                          │ for any residual lag from the wider windows, the RTS slope channel (already denoised by   │
│                          │ forward+backward evidence, lightly SG-smoothed with a fixed 5-tap order-2 kernel) is used │
│                          │ for a small conservative lead extrapolation (0.2*sg_half samples of slope), following the │
│                          │ successful Gen 46 lead design. This targets the untried Pareto point between the          │
│                          │ aggressive smoothing bank and the slope-gated lead.                                       │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0199                                                                                   │
