│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ pure_rts_slope_gated_lead                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current best (0.65) already contains the forward Kalman + RTS smoother + single       │
│                          │ zero-phase SG pass, but lacks any lag-compensation stage. The prior experiments show the  │
│                          │ trend-lead stage is the main lever on lag_error/responsiveness, but earlier versions      │
│                          │ contaminated it by blending a numerical gradient (`np.gradient`) with the RTS slope       │
│                          │ channel — the numerical gradient reintroduces exactly the ripple the SG cascade just      │
│                          │ removed, hurting slope_changes/false_reversals. This edit adds the minimal                │
│                          │ confidence-gated trend lead driven by the *pure RTS slope channel* (`smoothed_states[:,   │
│                          │ 1]`), which is already optimally smoothed by the RTS backward pass. No gradient is        │
│                          │ computed at all. The gate uses fixed constants anchored to the already-computed robust    │
│                          │ volatility scale `q_scale` (center 0.25·q_scale, temperature 0.15·q_scale) and a small    │
│                          │ lead of 0.5·sg_half·0.25, so the lag compensation is only applied where the smoothed      │
│                          │ slope exceeds the noise floor. Everything else in the file is untouched, making the score │
│                          │ delta attributable to this single change.                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0226                                                                                   │
