│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ triple_sg_gated_lead                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Key parameters in the current program: the SG smoothing bank (sg_half, h2), the slope     │
│                          │ blend weights (0.7 RTS / 0.3 gradient), the reversal-gate sigmoid thresholds (0.25/0.15 * │
│                          │ q_scale), and the lead gain (0.125*sg_half). The weakest metric is smoothness (0.30) with │
│                          │ elevated slope_changes (47.6) and false_reversals (34). Prior evidence shows noise        │
│                          │ reduction scales with smoothing-stage count (2 passes → 0.67, 3+ passes → smoothness      │
│                          │ 0.38, reversals 26-33). I therefore: (1) widen the second SG pass from sg_half//2 to      │
│                          │ (2*sg_half)//3 with a cubic kernel, (2) add a third short zero-phase pass (h3 = max(2,    │
│                          │ sg_half//3), quadratic) after lead compensation to suppress residual oscillation injected │
│                          │ by the lead term, and (3) tighten the reversal-gate threshold from 0.25 to 0.30*q_scale   │
│                          │ so weak slopes get less lead amplification (fewer false reversals), while keeping lead    │
│                          │ gain moderate so lag_error stays ~0.33. All passes remain zero-phase, so phase delay is   │
│                          │ unaffected.                                                                               │
