│ patch_description        │ Remove the gradient-slope blend in Stage 4 (set slope = slope_rts) as a minimal           │
│                          │ single-change mutation. The 0.3 gradient weight is the last identified noise leak:        │
│                          │ np.gradient(smoothed) reintroduces high-frequency content that the three-scale SG bank    │
│                          │ and RTS smoother already removed, and it feeds both the lead compensation and the         │
│                          │ reversal gate, inflating slope_changes and false_reversals while only marginally helping  │
│                          │ lag. Historically, pure RTS-slope variants held lag at 0.25–0.40 with best-in-class       │
│                          │ reversal counts. Everything else (q_scale2, gate constants, lead, Stage 4b final pass)    │
│                          │ stays verbatim so the score delta is attributable to the blend removal alone. Since       │
│                          │ slope_rts is the full magnitude of the RTS slope (previously down-weighted to 0.7), the   │
│                          │ lead compensation retains full strength, which also helps lag responsiveness — the        │
│                          │ gradient component's contribution to responsiveness was small because the gate attenuates │
│                          │ it in flat regions anyway.                                                                │
