│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single fixed-scale zero-phase SG polish, which forces one      │
│                          │ smoothing strength everywhere: it either over-smooths quiet regions (hurting              │
│                          │ lag/responsiveness) or under-smooths volatile ones (hurting smoothness and false          │
│                          │ reversals). The best prior generation (0.65, slope_changes 65.8, false_reversals 44.4)    │
│                          │ used a volatility-blended multi-scale SG polish, and the current program already computes │
│                          │ a local volatility proxy (r_arr) and keeps the stable fixed-Q Kalman + solve-based RTS    │
│                          │ smoother. This edit replaces the single-scale SG in Stage 2 with the multi-scale          │
│                          │ volatility-blended variant (soft Gaussian membership in volatility space centered at the  │
│                          │ 20/50/80 percentiles, three kernel scales), while keeping the confidence-gated trend lead │
│                          │ of Stage 3 intact. This targets the weakest metrics — smoothness (0.23) and reversals     │
│                          │ (45.4) — by widening the effective kernel only where local volatility genuinely demands   │
│                          │ it, without adding lag in quiet regions. Q remains strictly fixed at 0.05·q_scale² and    │
│                          │ the RTS gain stays solve-based, per confirmed prior findings; no Q-scheduling, no 3-state │
