│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ volatility_gated_cascade_and_softer_lead_gate                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current composition sits at 0.64 while the leaner Gen 3 anchor hit 0.65 with fewer    │
│                          │ slope changes (65.2 vs 66.8) and equal lag. The diagnosis: Stage 4's unconditional        │
│                          │ second-cascade SG pass over-smooths volatile regions, flattening genuine fast dynamics    │
│                          │ (adds lag + spurious reversals at trend re-entry), while Stage 5's sigmoid gate threshold │
│                          │ of 2.0 MAD is too conservative, leaving residual lag on genuine trends.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Two targeted fixes:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. **Volatility-gated cascade**: blend the cascaded (h2) result with the pre-cascade      │
│                          │ signal using a linear ramp in volatility-percentile space — full cascade weight only in   │
│                          │ the quietest 20-80th percentile band, zero cascade in genuinely volatile regions. This    │
│                          │ preserves the ripple-killing benefit where the signal is flat (fewer slope changes/false  │
│                          │ reversals) while keeping responsiveness exactly where lag matters.                        │
│                          │ 2. **Softer lead gate**: lower the sigmoid onset from 2.0 to 1.5 MAD units so confident   │
│                          │ trends get their lead compensation earlier, shaving lag_error without opening the gate to │
│                          │ noise (1.5 MAD is still well above the robust noise scale).                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Both changes are local, shape-safe, and preserve all existing degenerate-case guards.     │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
