│ patch_description        │ Key parameters identified in the current best (score 0.65): pure-RTS slope lead with gate │
│                          │ center `0.25·q_scale`, gate temperature `0.15·q_scale`, and lead amplitude                │
│                          │ `0.5·sg_half·0.25`. Prior evidence (Gen 77) indicates a 0.3 blend with a smoothed-level   │
│                          │ gradient slope improves responsiveness (lower lag_error, higher responsiveness_score)     │
│                          │ without materially hurting slope_changes or false_reversals, but that round confounded    │
│                          │ the blend with other changes. This variant keeps every gate/lead constant verbatim and    │
│                          │ changes a single variable: the Stage-3 slope channel now uses `slope = 0.7·slope_rts +    │
│                          │ 0.3·slope_grad`, where `slope_grad` is the robust central-difference gradient of the      │
│                          │ SG-smoothed level. This fuses the smoother's optimally-denoised slope (smoothness, few    │
│                          │ false reversals) with the zero-phase SG level's local gradient (responsiveness at genuine │
│                          │ turning points), isolating the blend effect for a clean single-variable score delta.      │
