│ patch_name               │ volatility_adaptive_sg_blend                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace Stage 3's fixed cascade of three SG passes (which the metrics show over-smooths:  │
│                          │ correlation 0.89, noise_reduction only 0.45, lag_error 0.42) with a volatility-adaptive   │
│                          │ blend. The current fixed wide-kernel bank smooths uniformly, degrading tracking accuracy  │
│                          │ and responsiveness, while keeping false reversals low. The recommendation: compute two    │
│                          │ zero-phase SG outputs (wide 2*sg_half and narrow sg_half//2) and blend them per-sample    │
│                          │ with a sigmoid of local volatility (convolved |diff|, as already computed for the Kalman  │
│                          │ R adaptation). In low-volatility regions the wide kernel dominates (smoothness, few slope │
│                          │ reversals); in high-volatility regions the narrow kernel takes over, restoring            │
│                          │ responsiveness and tracking of genuine dynamics. This targets the accuracy/lag deficits   │
│                          │ while preserving the reversal-penalty gains. Validate shapes after each stage to guard    │
│                          │ against the crash pattern seen in earlier generations.                                    │
