│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ multiscale_cascade_soft_lead                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current enhanced filter only has a single fixed-width zero-phase SG pass after the    │
│                          │ Kalman smoother. Prior generations showed two things: (a) a volatility-blended            │
│                          │ multi-scale kernel bank (short kernel for volatile regions = low lag; wide kernel for     │
│                          │ quiet regions = fewer spurious slope changes) plus a short second cascade dramatically    │
│                          │ reduced slope changes and false reversals without hurting the saturated correlation       │
│                          │ (0.97) or noise reduction (0.81→0.82), and (b) an aggressive trend-lead stage (high gate  │
│                          │ temperature / large lead magnitude) was the dominant mechanism injecting false reversals  │
│                          │ (45–66 at aggressive settings). Therefore I add the multi-scale blend + cascade exactly   │
│                          │ as validated, but a deliberately SOFT sigmoid-gated lead: temperature                     │
│                          │ 0.10*q_scale2-equivalent and lead magnitude scaled to 0.4*sg_half*0.25, so the lead only  │
│                          │ fires on statistically significant slopes (opens the gate slowly, small magnitude),       │
│                          │ cutting reversals below 34 while preserving lag/NR gains.                                 │
