│ patch_description        │ The bottleneck is slope changes (62.8) and false reversals (43.8) — smoothness — while    │
│                          │ correlation (0.97) and noise reduction (0.81) have headroom to trade. The                 │
│                          │ volatility-gated blend's widest scale (2*sg_half) still passes too much residual          │
│                          │ oscillation in high-volatility regions where those spurious reversals originate. Widening │
│                          │ the widest candidate scale to 3*sg_half suppresses them where volatility gating already   │
│                          │ activates that branch (quiet regions keep the narrow scale, preserving responsiveness).   │
│                          │ To offset the added corner attenuation/lag, slightly raise the slope-lead compensation    │
│                          │ from 0.12 to 0.18 of the look-ahead — well below the historically safe 0.25 fraction that │
│                          │ scored lag_error 0.35 in the prior lineage, so lag should remain acceptable. This mirrors │
│                          │ the "Gen 2" lineage behavior (48 slope changes) while retaining the volatility gating     │
│                          │ that protects lag (0.27) and correlation (0.97).                                          │
