│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ volatility_scheduled_q                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current implementation uses a fixed process-noise Q = 0.05*q_scale²*I. This forces a  │
│                          │ single rigidity/flexibility tradeoff across the entire signal: too rigid in volatile      │
│                          │ regions (lag, missed genuine dynamics) and too flexible in quiet regions (noise-induced   │
│                          │ wobble, false reversals — slope_changes 65.8, false_reversals 44.4). The first prior      │
│                          │ program showed that volatility-scheduling Q (rigid where quiet, flexible where volatile)  │
│                          │ directly targets these two metrics while preserving responsiveness. This edit computes a  │
│                          │ per-sample q_arr scaled by normalized local volatility and uses q_arr inside the Kalman   │
│                          │ predict step, keeping everything else (RTS smoother, multi-scale SG, confidence-gated     │
│                          │ trend lead) byte-identical so the score delta isolates the Q-scheduling effect. Costs     │
│                          │ O(n) extra and no latency.                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
