│                          │ Following the recommendation, I add a light, unconditional third zero-phase               │
│                          │ Savitzky-Golay pass after the slope-lead compensation, using half-width `h3 = max(2,      │
│                          │ sg_half // 3)` and order 2 — narrow enough that the added lag is negligible, but          │
│                          │ sufficient to suppress the residual ripple the lead compensation reintroduces. It reuses  │
│                          │ the existing `_sg_smooth` helper (mirrored reflect-padding plus degenerate-length         │
│                          │ fallback), and the final end-aligned trim is guarded with a `len(out) >= output_length`   │
