│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ slope_conditional_quiet_region_polish                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Apply an unconditional small SG polish only in quiet regions (small slope magnitude),     │
│                          │ then a localized slope-magnitude-conditional smoothing pass using the existing hysteresis │
│                          │ machinery with a stricter slope gate. The key idea: slope changes (79.6) and false        │
│                          │ reversals (58.4) come from residual dithering in flat regions where |slope| is small      │
│                          │ relative to a robust slope scale. Smooth only there with a small zero-phase order-2 SG    │
│                          │ kernel (window 5), blending via np.where, so genuine transitions keep their               │
│                          │ responsiveness. This avoids the failure mode of extra global SG passes (Gens 82-85) by    │
│                          │ conditioning on local slope magnitude rather than applying everywhere.                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0063                                                                                   │
