│ patch_description        │ The current best score (0.65) is dominated by false_reversals (42.2) and slope_changes    │
│                          │ (62.2), while lag (0.27) and correlation (0.97) are already good. The Stage-4 lead        │
│                          │ consumes the RTS slope state polished only by a 5-tap kernel; residual ripple in the      │
│                          │ slope channel is the main injector of spurious reversals through the sigmoid gate.        │
│                          │ Replace the fixed 5-tap slope polish with a wider, zero-phase SG kernel of half-width     │
│                          │ `sg_half // 2 + 1` (still short relative to the window, so responsiveness is preserved),  │
│                          │ and slightly raise the gate center (1.5 -> 1.75) so only more statistically significant   │
│                          │ slopes open the gate. This suppresses noise-driven lead spikes without materially raising │
│                          │ lag, since the gate remains ~0 in quiet regions (no added delay there) and full on        │
│                          │ confident trends.                                                                         │
